   "definition_quote": "At each round $t$, a learner chooses an action $x_t \\in \\cX$ and observes the reward $r_t = \\theta^\\top x_t + \\eta_t$, where $\\eta_t$ is a symmetric and independent noise. ... We say a random variable, $\\eta$, has $\\alpha$-heavy-tail for some $\\alpha>0$, if ... $\\Pr(|\\eta| > y) \\le \\frac{1}{y^\\alpha}$."
