    "label": "thm:regret",
    "number": "Theorem 6",
    "quote": "Suppose a linear bandit instance, $(\\cX, \\theta)$, has $\\alpha$-heavy-tail noise for some $\\alpha > 0$. Fix $\\varepsilon \\in (0, 1)$. Let $\\tilde{n} = \\lceil \\max\\{C, \\big(16\\log(2T/\\delta)\\bigr)^{1/\\varepsilon}, (2\\cdot4^{2/\\alpha}\\log(4/\\delta))^{\\frac{1}{1-\\varepsilon}}\\} \\rceil$ ... Then, Algorithm \\ref{alg2} with input $(\\cA, \\delta, \\varepsilon, \\tilde{n})$ enjoys a regret bound \\[\\tilde{n} \\cdot R(d, T/\\tilde{n}, \\delta)\\] with probability at least $1 - 2\\delta$."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Pseudo-regret holding w.p. 1-2delta. Generic reduction; expression involves the base algorithm's regret function R."
